  "notes": "Official cause code is TBD in FORM-366 fields (block 13 shows '8' as a numeric code, not one of the standard A-E/X cause letters, so cause_code/category are kept as provisional per rule 4). Failure was discovered retrospectively via failure analysis; the valve had not been operated since refueling outage L2R18, roughly two years prior, establishing a past inoperability condition for the full cycle. No BACKED_UP_BY edges emitted: B train of SLC was also affected by concurrent DG inoperabilities per LCO 3.8.1, and narrative does not state B train remained operable throughout — it is discussed only as an LCO-driven consequence, not a stated available backup. Previous occurrence stub uses Part 21 notification date/company as the closest identifiable prior-occurrence record since no formal LER number is given in the narrative."
